_ai.operation.name":"execute_tool","io.tool":"command_execution","io.input":"{\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc \\\"curl -L --max-time 15 -s 'https://api.github.com/repos/react-hook-form/react-hook-form/commits?path=src/logic/updateFieldArrayRootError.ts&per_page=10' | rg -n 'sha|message|html_url' | head -40\\\"\"}","io.output":"{\"output\":\"3:    \\\"sha\\\": \\\"645478be493ee2d992275db6bf7bb98d64de459b\\\",\\n16:      \\\"message\\\": \\\"🐞 fix FieldArray errors overriding nested fields (#13476)\\\\n\\\\n* Initial plan\\\\n\\\\n* fix: preserve nested field array errors when root error and trigger coexist\\\\n\\\\nWhen a resolver returns mixed errors (both root-level and nested indexed\\\\nerrors) for a field array, calling trigger() alongside a field array action\\\\n(like remove()) could cause nested field errors to be wiped out.\\\\n\\\\nRoot cause: executeSchemaAndUpdateState() was calling updateFieldArrayRootError()\\\\nfor all plain-object field array errors. updateFieldArrayRootError() used\\\\nconvertToArrayPayload() to coerce the existing errors, but when those errors\\\\nwere already a plain object (set by the useFieldArray useEffect), this wrapped\\\\nthe entire plain object as index 0 of an array — causing all the\\\\ncorrectly-indexed nested errors to become inaccessible.\\\\n\\\\nFix 1 (createFormControl.ts): Only call updateFieldArrayRootError() for\\\\nfield array errors that are root-only plain objects (no numeric/index keys).\\\\nWhen the error has numeric keys (mixed root + nested), set it directly so\\\\nboth root info (via .type/.message) and nested errors (via [i]) are preserved.\\\\n\\\\nFix 2 (updateFieldArrayRootError.ts): Replace convertToArrayPayload() with\\\\nan Array.isArray() check so that non-array existing errors are not wrapped.\\\\nThis prevents a scenario where a second trigger() with a root-only error\\\\nwraps a previously-set plain object, losing its nested entries.\\\\n\\\\n* update lint\\\\n\\\\n---------\\\\n\\\\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\\\\nCo-authored-by: bill <bluebill1049@hotmail.com>\\\",\\n18:        \\\"sha\\\": \\\"ed81b5524a3a046c2df176acb177cf9e11d069cb\\\",\\n27:        \\\"payload\\\": \\\"tree ed81b5524a3a046c2df176acb177cf9e11d069cb\\\\nparent 889c7523d6c5c68bfc3c78142782cb0a3310729d\\\\nauthor Copilot <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com> 1779603508 +1000\\\\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779603508 +1000\\\\n\\\\n🐞 fix FieldArray errors overriding nested fields (#13476)\\\\n\\\\n* Initial plan\\\\n\\\\n* fix: preserve nested field array errors when root error and trigger coexist\\\\n\\\\nWhen a resolver returns mixed errors (both root-level and nested indexed\\\\nerrors) for a field array, calling trigger() alongside a field array action\\\\n(like remove()) could cause nested field errors to be wiped out.\\\\n\\\\nRoot cause: executeSchemaAndUpdateState() was calling updateFieldArrayRootError()\\\\nfor all plain-object field array errors. updateFieldArrayRootError() used\\\\nconvertToArrayPayload() to coerce the existing errors, but when those errors\\\\nwere already a plain object (set by the useFieldArray useEffect), this wrapped\\\\nthe entire plain object as index 0 of an array — causing all the\\\\ncorrectly-indexed nested errors to become inaccessible.\\\\n\\\\nFix 1 (createFormControl.ts): Only call updateFieldArrayRootError() for\\\\nfield array errors that are root-only plain objects (no numeric/index keys).\\\\nWhen the error has numeric keys (mixed root + nested), set it directly so\\\\nboth root info (via .type/.message) and nested errors (via [i]) are preserved.\\\\n\\\\nFix 2 (updateFieldArrayRootError.ts): Replace convertToArrayPayload() with\\\\nan Array.isArray() check so that non-array existing errors are not wrapped.\\\\nThis prevents a scenario where a second trigger() with a root-only error\\\\nwraps a previously-set plain object, losing its nested entries.\\\\n\\\\n* update lint\